Incognita data licence
======================

The code in this repository is licensed under Apache-2.0 (LICENSE). The data listed below are the project's own work
and are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Cite Incognita (CITATION.cff) and, for EXFOR-derived content, the
EXFOR library.

Data covered by CC BY 4.0
-------------------------
- library/v0.1/                      predictions: capture curves, MACS, rates, channel tables, intervals
- docs/registry/                     frozen prospective predictions and their manifests
- docs/release/exam/, docs/release/uq/, docs/release/expected/, incognita/bench/tracks/, incognita/bench/data/
                                     exam cells, frozen predictions, expected tables, benchmark tracks
- docs/release/MEASURE_NEXT.csv      the measure-next ranking
- data/curation/                     the curation register (decisions about EXFOR datasets)
- models/data/kadonis_keep.csv       which compiled MACS entries rest on experimental data (flags only, no values)

Third-party content inside those files, and its terms
-----------------------------------------------------
- EXFOR (IAEA Nuclear Data Section and the NRDC network). Exam targets and curation evidence are derived from EXFOR
  points. The EXFOR Master File is distributed by the IAEA under CC BY 4.0. Cite: N. Otuka et al., Nucl. Data Sheets
  120 (2014) 272.
- RIPL (IAEA, RIPL-3 / RIPL-4): parsed parameters (for example physics/hf/gamma/ggnorm_ripl3.csv and the resonance
  spacings D0 used by the model). IAEA-NDS terms: scientific reuse with attribution.
- Nuclear masses: AME2020 (W.J. Huang et al., Chinese Phys. C 45 (2021) 030002; M. Wang et al., ibid. 030003) and
  theory tables distributed through RIPL.
- NUBASE2020 half-lives (measure-next ranking): F.G. Kondev et al., Chinese Phys. C 45 (2021) 030001.
- TALYS (MIT licence, A. Koning et al.): the engine is a port; physics/hf/NOTICE-TALYS.md reproduces the licence. The
  TALYS structure database is not redistributed; users download it.
- Compiled measured MACS values: 21 nuclides of the ANCHORED tier are scaled to compiled measured 30 keV MACS values,
  so their macs30_mb reproduces those values by construction. The compiled values themselves are not distributed as a
  column.
- The Atlas of Neutron Resonances (S.F. Mughabghab) was used during development for resonance counts that set the
  resolved-resonance upper bound (column resolved_upper_ev of the capture table). No Atlas values are distributed.

No evaluated nuclear-data library values (ENDF/B, JENDL, JEFF, TENDL, CENDL, BROND, FENDL, IRDFF, BRUSLIB cross
sections) are distributed in this repository. Scripts that compare against them read files the user downloads.
docs/data-licensing.md records each source, its version and its licence status.
